---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SocialShare from "../../components/SocialShare.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="How to Use the Salary Tax Calculator: A Worked Example"
    description="Step-by-step guide to using our Pakistan salary tax calculator. Includes a worked example, FBR tax slabs for 2026-27, and salary slip tips."
>
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <header class="mb-8">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-2">
                Published: October 17, 2026 · Last Updated: October 24, 2026 ·
                By <a href="/about/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline"
                    >Khuram Shahzad</a
                >
            </p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-3">
                How to Use the Salary Tax Calculator: A Worked Example
            </h1>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600">
                Calculate your exact take-home salary after FBR income tax and
                EOBI deductions for Tax Year 2027 (FY 2026-27). No signup, no
                download, 100% private.
            </p>
        </header>

        <section class="space-y-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            <p>
                Every salaried person in Pakistan asks the same question at the
                start of each tax year: "How much tax will I pay, and what's my
                actual take-home salary?"
            </p>
            <p>
                Doing the math manually is tedious — multiple slabs, EOBI
                deductions, yearly vs monthly confusion. That's why most people
                either ask HR or just accept whatever figure appears on their
                salary slip.
            </p>
            <p>
                Our{" "}
                <a
                    href="/tools/salary-tax-calculator/"
                    class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium"
                >
                    free Salary Tax Calculator
                </a>{" "}
                does the whole thing in seconds. This guide shows how to use it, how
                the FBR slabs work, and what to check on your salary slip.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">
                Quick Answer: How to Use the Salary Tax Calculator
            </h2>
            <p>
                Go to our{" "}
                <a
                    href="/tools/salary-tax-calculator/"
                    class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium"
                >
                    Salary Tax Calculator
                </a>{" "}
                and:
            </p>
            <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2">
                <li>Enter your monthly gross salary (e.g. PKR 150,000)</li>
                <li>
                    Leave "Include EOBI" checked if your employer deducts it
                </li>
                <li>Click "Calculate Tax"</li>
                <li>
                    See your monthly tax, yearly tax, net take-home, and slab
                    breakdown
                </li>
            </ol>
            <p>
                The entire calculation happens in your browser — your salary
                data never leaves your device.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">
                What the Calculator Shows
            </h2>
            <p>When you enter your monthly salary, the tool gives you:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                <li>
                    <strong>Monthly tax:</strong> What gets deducted from your salary
                    each month
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Yearly tax:</strong> The total FBR income tax on your
                    annual income
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Monthly take-home:</strong> Your net salary after tax
                    and EOBI
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Yearly take-home:</strong> Total amount you receive in
                    a year
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Taxable annual income:</strong> The base on which tax
                    is calculated
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Your tax slab:</strong> Which FBR bracket you fall into
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Tax saving tips:</strong> FBR-approved ways to reduce
                    your tax
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">What Is a Salary Slip?</h2>
            <p>
                A <strong>salary slip</strong> (also called pay slip or payslip) is
                a document your employer gives you every month showing:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                <li>Basic salary</li>
                <li>Allowances (house rent, medical, transport)</li>
                <li>Deductions (income tax, EOBI, provident fund)</li>
                <li>Net pay (what actually lands in your bank account)</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                When you use our{" "}
                <a
                    href="/tools/salary-tax-calculator/"
                    class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium"
                >
                    Salary Tax Calculator
                </a>
                , you can cross-check the "income tax" line on your salary slip to
                make sure your employer is deducting the correct amount.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">
                Common Mistakes to Avoid
            </h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                <li>
                    <strong>Confusing monthly and annual slab:</strong> Your slab
                    is decided by your <em>annual</em> taxable income, not monthly.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Forgetting EOBI:</strong> If your salary is above the
                    EOBI wage limit, EOBI is deducted monthly and reduces your take-home.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Not checking your salary slip:</strong> Employers sometimes
                    miscalculate. Compare your salary slip against our calculator.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Ignoring tax credits:</strong> Investments in VPS, life
                    insurance, and certain donations can reduce your tax. Use our{
                        " "
                    }
                    <a
                        href="/blog/how-to-save-tax-pakistan/"
                        class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium"
                    >
                        tax saving guide
                    </a>{" "}
                    to learn more.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">
                Why Use an Online Salary Tax Calculator?
            </h2>
            <p>
                Manual calculation is possible but error-prone. Here's why an
                online calculator is better:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                <li><strong>Instant:</strong> Results in under a second</li>
                <li><strong>Accurate:</strong> Uses the latest FBR slabs</li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Complete breakdown:</strong> Shows every line item
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Private:</strong> Runs in your browser, no data sent anywhere
                </li>
                <li><strong>Free:</strong> No signup, no limits, no ads</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">
                Frequently Asked Questions
            </h2>
            <div class="space-y-4 mt-3">
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        What is the tax-free income limit in Pakistan?
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        For Tax Year 2027, the tax-free limit for salaried
                        individuals is PKR 600,000 per year (PKR 50,000 per
                        month).
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        Are these tax slabs accurate for 2026-27?
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        Yes. These slabs are based on the Finance Act 2026 and
                        apply to salaried individuals for Tax Year 2027 (July
                        2026 – June 2027).
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        Does the calculator include the 9% surcharge?
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        No. The 9% surcharge has been abolished for salaried
                        individuals in the Finance Act 2026.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        Is my salary data stored anywhere?
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        No. All calculations happen in your browser. Your salary
                        information never leaves your device.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        Can I calculate tax for a different tax year?
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        Our calculator currently supports Tax Year 2027 (FY
                        2026-27). Future years will be added as FBR announces
                        new slabs.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        Does the calculator work on mobile?
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        Yes. The tool works on any device — laptop, tablet,
                        phone, or desktop.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Final Thoughts</h2>
            <p>
                Knowing your exact take-home salary is important for budgeting
                and financial planning. Our{" "}
                <a
                    href="/tools/salary-tax-calculator/"
                    class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium"
                >
                    Salary Tax Calculator
                </a>{" "}
                makes this easy — no formula, no manual math, no signup.
            </p>
            <p>
                For related guides, check out{" "}
                <a
                    href="/blog/salary-tax-pakistan/"
                    class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium"
                >
                    how salary tax works in Pakistan
                </a>{" "}
                and{" "}
                <a
                    href="/blog/how-to-save-tax-pakistan/"
                    class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium"
                >
                    7 legal ways to save tax
                </a>.
            </p>
        </section>

        <SocialShare
